    "dashboardEvidence::trait-1": "You rated 66; they landed at 64. Straight read. But effectiveness 81 against effort 30 says it lands without you grinding — so the extra rounds are not for them.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t1-q01": "Being led by you costs them little in this trait. Notice you did not know that, and kept explaining anyway.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t1-q02": "Effectiveness at 81 with almost no visible effort. This is the part you are getting right and still treating as unfinished.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t1-q03": "They see that it already landed. You are the one who kept the room open.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s1": "Compass 48 against your 65. Expectations up front are the one place your explaining would actually pay, and it is not showing up there.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s2": "Effectiveness 99 and effort 21. They rarely have to ask twice. So who is the second explanation for?",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s3": "Effectiveness 100. You adapt to the person in front of you and rated yourself 67 for it. You undersell the thing you actually do.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s4": "Your floor. Compass 40, and you called it 63. Complex decisions get explained — they just do not arrive as something anyone can act on.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s5": "Effectiveness 97. They know what success looks like. What they do not have is permission to judge whether they hit it.",
    "dashboardEvidence::trait-2": "Effort 90, effectiveness 74. They watch you work at direction more than they feel it arrive. You said 84; they said 79. Close enough to stop arguing.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t2-q01": "They see the effort. That is not the compliment it sounds like — visible effort means the work is still on your side of the table.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t2-q02": "Purpose lands. People feel the why around you. Own it without appending the qualifier.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t2-q03": "They see how hard you push direction. What they cannot see is why it needs pushing that hard.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t2-s1": "Effort 100, effectiveness 40, and you rated it 60. You already suspected this one. Saying it more often has not made it clearer.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t2-s2": "Compass 83 and you guessed 85. You read this one accurately. Rare — most of your accuracy is on the things going well.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t2-s3": "Effectiveness 95, effort 68. You adjust priorities well and know it. Nothing to fix here, which will bother you.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t2-s4": "Effort 98, effectiveness 62, you called it 83. Maximum output, partial landing. That is the whole shape of your explaining.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t2-s5": "Compass 93. You see trouble coming and prepare them for it. Then you handle the hard piece yourself anyway.",
    "dashboardEvidence::trait-3": "Effort 90, effectiveness 28. The widest split you have. You knew it was bad — you rated 40 — and you still absorbed the schedule instead of renegotiating it.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t3-q01": "Under deadline, being led by you means watching someone work very hard and feeling almost none of it. That is the cost, present tense.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t3-q02": "They credit the effort. Effort is not the deliverable and you would not accept this trade from anyone reporting to you.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t3-q03": "They see you eating pressure that was never yours to eat. Nobody learns to carry a deadline by watching you swallow one.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t3-s1": "Effectiveness 17. Your floor across everything. You take the timeline as given, then take the work back to make it true.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t3-s2": "Effort 100, effectiveness 31. When the date moves, they hear a lot and learn little. Context is not the same as a decision.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t3-s3": "Effort 100, effectiveness 19. You are not removing blockers. You are absorbing them, which looks identical from your desk and nothing like it from theirs.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t3-s4": "Compass 50. The team meets its commitments at half strength — because commitments belong to you, not them.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t3-s5": "Trust at 56, and you guessed 59. You know the follow-through is thin. You keep buying it back with your own hands."
