    "selfAssessment::default": "You go first, then they do. Yours has your name on it; theirs never will.",
    "selfAssessment::survey-open": "Rate the ordinary week, not the week you were sharp. You tend to be generous about effort and vague about what actually landed.",
    "teamAssessment::default": "Send it to the people who see you when the deadline is ugly, not the ones who only see you in the good rooms.",
    "dashboardEvidence::trait-1": "Effectiveness 81 on effort 30. All that circling you thought was doing the work? They didn't even register it as work.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t1-q01": "Being led by you here feels easy and clear to them. The part you sweat over isn't the part they feel.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t1-q02": "This is the column you're getting right. Read it fully before you go hunting for the flaw in it.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t1-q03": "What you can't see: clarity arrives long before you stop talking. You could stop halfway and they'd still have it.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s1": "You had this at 65, they're at 48. The expectations do get clear — just not before the work starts.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s2": "Effectiveness 99. They almost never come back for a second pass, and you guessed 67. That underrating is its own kind of tell.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s3": "A perfect hundred. You meet people where they are and don't even count it as effort — that's the collaborative instinct showing up on paper.",
