    "selfAssessment::default": "You go first, then they do. Their answers come to you as a pattern with no names on it — that protection is deliberate.",
    "selfAssessment::survey-open": "Answer for the ordinary week, not the day you were at your best. The distance between those two is where your people actually live.",
    "teamAssessment::default": "Send it yourself, to the people who see you under pressure — not only the ones who already agree with your read.",
    "dashboardEvidence::trait-1": "They say it lands and costs you almost nothing. You believed repetition was what made it work; they are telling you it was never the repetition.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t1-q01": "Being led by you here feels light to them — high result, low visible strain. Take that in properly before you go looking for the flaw.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t1-q02": "This is one of the things you are genuinely getting right. You are allowed to sit with that for longer than a second.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t1-q03": "Here they see the effort you thought was invisible. What you read as care, they register as work being done at them.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s1": "Expectations before the start land at 60 for them and 65 for you — close. The upfront framing is where their confidence is thinnest, not the follow-up.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s2": "They almost never need to come back and ask. You rated this modestly; they rated it near perfect. Your explaining was never the reason it landed.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s3": "You meet people where they are, and they feel it completely. You scored yourself well below what they gave you — notice how you underweight your own reach.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s4": "Complex decisions explained so they can act: their weakest point in this room. They understand the reasoning. What's missing is the call at the end of it.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t1-s5": "They know what success looks like in their roles, more surely than you believed. That clarity is yours — and it makes the withheld decisions louder, not quieter.",
    "dashboardEvidence::trait-2": "They see the effort going in at 90 and feel 74 of it arrive. Saying it often is not the same as it being understood, and you have been treating those as one thing.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t2-q01": "They watch you work hard at direction. Most of it reaches them — some of it stays visible as effort rather than becoming clarity they can carry.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t2-q02": "They feel the purpose behind the work. That connection is real and you built it; hold onto it as you read the rest.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t2-q03": "What they see: the direction is well-said, not always well-held. Frequency has been doing the work you thought comprehension was doing.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t2-s1": "Maximum effort, and only 40 lands on where the team is headed. You rated yourself the same 60 — you sense this one, and you've been answering it with volume.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t2-s2": "Connecting daily work to purpose: you and they agree it's strong. This is the room where the why genuinely arrives.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t2-s3": "Revisiting priorities lands at 95 for them. You are willing to change your mind in public — that is more rare than you treat it.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t2-s4": "You rated this 83; they feel 62. They see enormous effort spent on their line of sight and still can't quite trace their work to the whole.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t2-s5": "Anticipating what's coming: 98 effective, your strongest statement anywhere. You see the road ahead for them. The question is who else is being taught to.",
    "dashboardEvidence::trait-3": "Effort 90, effectiveness 28. This is the widest gap you have, and it is the exact shape of absorbing schedule pressure alone instead of renegotiating it.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t3-q01": "Under deadline, they watch you strain and feel almost nothing change. That is a hard thing to read about yourself, and it is what carrying it alone looks like from outside.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t3-q02": "Even here, they credit the effort. They know you are trying to shield them — they just cannot feel the shield holding.",
    "dashboardSignal::sent-t3-q03": "They see the cost you pay and the result they don't get. You rated yourself 40 here; you knew. Knowing has not been enough.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t3-s1": "Realistic timelines and delivered commitments: 17 effective. You rated it 33 — you already suspected. A promise made alone gets broken alone.",
    "dashboardEvidence::t3-s2": "Full effort on communicating shifts, 31 felt. They hear about the change; they don't get told early enough to do anything with it.",
